#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# part

#% text
# `part(t, i)`, written `t[i]`, gives the `i`-th element of the list `t` (the `i`-th argument of a term).

#% text
# `part(t, i, j, ...)`, written `t[i, j, ...]`, goes down one level per index.

#% text
# `part(t, span(i, j))`, written `t[i:j]`, gives the elements from position `i` to `j`; a list of indices, `t[[i1, i2, ...]]`, gives several.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Indices start at 1. Negative indices count from the end: `t[-1]` is the last element.

#% item
# `t[0]` is the head of a term.

#% item
# An index past the end gives a failure `failure(index, i, n)` naming the index and the length.

#% item
# On an association, `a[k]` looks up the key `k`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
xs = [a, b, c, d, e]
xs[2]
#% output
#= b

#% cell
xs[-1]
#% output
#= e

#% cell
xs[2:4]
#% output
#= [b, c, d]

#% cell
[[1, 2], [3, 4]][2, 1]
#% output
#= 3

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Several positions at once:

#% cell
xs[[1, 3, 5]]
#% output
#= [a, c, e]

#% text
# A whole column of a matrix: every row, then one index:

#% cell
m = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]
map(row => row[2], m)
#% output
#= [2, 5]

#% text
# The head and arguments of a term:

#% cell
[f(x, y)[0], f(x, y)[2]]
#% output
#= [f, y]

#% text
# A key of an association:

#% cell
assoc("mass" -> 2.5, "charge" -> -1)["mass"]
#% output
#= 2.5

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The value from a pair `[time, value]`, as the scripts unpack the results of `timing`:

#% cell
r = timing(sum(range(1000)))
r[2]
#% output
#= 500500

#% text
# The end of a solution's domain, from the nested structure of the solution:

#% cell
s = n_dsolve([y'(t) == -y(t), y(0) == 1], y, [t, 0, 2])
(y /. s)[2]
#% output
#= [0.0, 2.0]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `first` and `last` are `part` with 1 and -1:

#% cell
[first(xs) === xs[1], last(xs) === xs[-1]]
#% output
#= [true, true]

#% text
# `take` is a span from 1:

#% cell
take(xs, 3) === xs[1:3]
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# An index past the end:

#% cell
xs[9]
#% output
#! failure(index, 9, 5)

#% text
# Index 0 is the head, not the first element:

#% cell
xs[0]
#% output
#= list

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `first`, `last`, `take`, `position`, `lookup`
